- Story & Context: At the swamp-edge clearing outside Okefenokee, the Barrow-Delmonico wedding reception had degenerated into an armed feud until young Wayne Barrow shoved his thumb into a leaking kerosene drum, kicked on his bass rig, and locked the feuding clans into a staggering, three-note drop-tuned loop. Over the stench of scorched radiator fluid and crushed cotton candy, the bride’s trapeze-flyer uncles picked up their brass to drop clipped offbeats right into the teeth of Wayne's southern pentatonic crawl until every revolver was lowered in rhythm. By the third unbroken hour of the jam, the presiding rural preacher was found collapsed in the sawdust with his eyes wide open in an ecstatic stupor, whispering the groom's improvised ring-vow over the din: "Tie your ribs to the rigging and swallow the seed."
